  (:adr/body "2026-09-01. What landed, what did not, and where the next session starts.

## Shipped and verified live

**Discovery surfaces on x402.nexus.** /.well-known/mcp.json, POST /mcp
(JSON-RPC), /openapi.json, /skill.md, /faucet, /sitemap.xml, robots.txt with a
Sitemap line, and canonical + OpenGraph + JSON-LD in the head. Unrouted paths
answer 404; they used to answer the index page with 200.

**The faucet gate**, as a pure decision (nexus.faucet). Draws are counted per
WebAuthn credential rather than per address or IP, and the document says
plainly that a passkey proves ONE AUTHENTICATOR, not one person. It verifies
nothing itself -- webauthn.adapters.edge already does that in production at
auth.itonami.cloud -- and it issues the spend grant separately from the
tokens, because folding them into one success is how a caller comes to believe
it was paid.

**Four SDKs, published and installed back from their registries:**

    npm        @com-kotobalabs/x402@0.1.0
    PyPI       com-kotobalabs-x402@0.1.0
    crates.io  com-kotobalabs-x402@0.1.0
    Go         github.com/kotoba-lang/x402-sdk/packages/go@v0.1.0

Each was installed into an empty project and run against the live facilitator,
not merely uploaded. All four printed base-sepolia, 1000 units, domain USDC/2,
chainId 84532.

**Two detectors**, both shown to go red before being trusted:
verify-advertised-surfaces (a document naming an endpoint the host does not
serve) and verify-x402-offer-domain (a live offer whose EIP-712 domain is not
the token's own).

**A gasless settlement proof** (scripts/x402-gasless-settle-proof.cljs) that
builds and signs the transaction and stops before sending, and the bridge leg
(scripts/sepolia-to-base-bridge.cljs).

