## One defect class, met eleven times

A thing that could not measure returned what a thing that measured and found
nothing returns. Every instance below was found by an attempt, never by
reading the code:

  - four endpoints reported live because the worker answered 200 to every path
  - a manifest advertising zero tools, from a renderer called in the
    JSON-to-EDN direction
  - a tool returning Cloudflare's 522 text as its result, inside a 200
  - a call to a function that exists nowhere, compiling with the same
    :undeclared-var warning as three benign forward references
  - a detector scanning one network of two and exiting 0, because the other
    listing is POST-only and answers a GET with 404
  - a registrable-domain helper threaded with ->> so every host compared equal
  - ~/.cargo/credentials.toml present and reported as authenticated; the
    publish returned 403
  - npm 404 for ten minutes after a publish that exited 0
  - `$?` reading tail's exit code rather than the check's
  - a docs verifier run in a sparse worktree reporting 528 absent files
  - a closing check reporting exit=1 for a script that was not in the checkout

## Two regressions, same cause

The per-network EIP-712 domain and the sitemap's js/Response fix both went
live and then came back. Both were DEPLOYED FROM A WORKTREE CARRYING
UNCOMMITTED WORK, so live diverged from main, and a later deploy -- itself
correct, shipping exactly what main said -- reverted them silently. The
wrangler guard checks a checkout is not BEHIND origin/main; it cannot see that
one is ahead in ways nobody committed.

Land before deploying. Both fixes are now on main.

## Gaps, in the order they block things

1. **Three tokens are in this transcript** -- npm, crates.io, PyPI. All three
   were used and all three should be revoked. The pattern that avoids this is
   the one the rest of this workspace uses: the value lives in kagi, a tool
   reads one item by a known identifier, and it never enters the agent's
   context. 1Password could not do that here: the desktop app's CLI
   integration is off, so op signin, op read and op item get all fail
   identically.

2. **Testnet gas.** Base Sepolia cannot be mined -- difficulty 0x0, miner
   0x4200000000000000000000000000000000000011, eth_mining unimplemented. Its
   ETH is minted by the bridge, and Sepolia L1 ETH can be earned by hashing at
   pk910's CryptoNight faucet, whose captcha module has requiredForStart:
   true. One human gesture, then scripts/sepolia-to-base-bridge.cljs carries
   it across. One settlement costs 0.00000144 ETH.

3. **The faucet cannot be claimed.** Verification is not wired; it needs a
   client registered at auth.itonami.cloud, which has no dynamic registration
   endpoint. /faucet says claimable: false and names no claim URL it cannot
   serve.

4. **com-kotobalabs is an organisation only on npm.** The PyPI and GitHub
   organisations do not exist, so there the name is only a name. Owner
   accepted personal ownership for now. Creating them is account creation and
   needs the owner in a browser.

5. **Three standing findings on etzhayyim**, from the estate run: two
   atproto.etzhayyim.com .well-known paths answer Cloudflare 1033, and
   mcp.etzhayyim.com does not resolve in DNS although
   orgs/kotoba-lang/app-agentgateway declares that host.

## Resume point

    nbb --classpath \".:scripts/nbb_compat\" scripts/sepolia-to-base-bridge.cljs

Exits 2 while unfunded and says what is needed. After a faucet draw it builds
the deposit that carries Sepolia ETH to Base Sepolia, holding back its own
gas. Then the x402 buyer at 0x38C2229589e2097486b4a3390f557E84cB69F30c can
make the first autonomous purchase, and pay.x402's `exact` path means it needs
USDC and no ETH.

## Not touched

The shared superproject checkout is 46 commits behind origin/main and another
session holds its index.lock; it was left alone rather than forced. Two open
PRs on nexus-x402 (#25 gateway-bare-prefix-challenges, #20
facilitator-advertises-only-settleable-schemes) and eight cleanup-* branches
belong to other sessions. One nexus worktree (nexus-faucet) and its
agent/testnet-faucet branch are another session's. One uncommitted diff found
in my own seo worktree was archived to
.git/stash-archive-20260901/seo-worktree-js-response-fix.patch before removal,
even though the same fix had already landed as f4c61c74.

## The constraint has not moved

The catalog holds 25 priced resources across 7 sellers and external payments
remain at one, for $0.001, on 2026-08-14. Everything shipped today makes the
shop easier to find, easier to call and easier to build against. None of it is
evidence that anyone will buy.")))
